{"uid":"21f05ea7b1da176d","name":"test_a_row_already_being_replayed_is_refused","fullName":"tests.test_routes_system_effects#test_a_row_already_being_replayed_is_refused","historyId":"b8c92eb56012bca6253dc47ae281f4ba","time":{"start":1793026514367,"stop":1793026514382,"duration":15},"description":"The row is claimed before sending, so a second caller cannot deliver twice.\n\n    Without the claim both callers read ``open``, both POST, and the operator gets two\n    deliveries for one request — the opposite of what a recovery tool should do.\n\n    The claimed state is asserted directly rather than by driving two real requests: a\n    nested in-handler call would test the test harness's re-entrancy, not the database\n    predicate that actually arbitrates.\n    ","descriptionHtml":"<p>The row is claimed before sending, so a second caller cannot deliver twice.</p>\n<pre><code>Without the claim both callers read ``open``, both POST, and the operator gets two\ndeliveries for one request — the opposite of what a recovery tool should do.\n\nThe claimed state is asserted directly rather than by driving two real requests: a\nnested in-handler call would test the test harness's re-entrancy, not the database\npredicate that actually arbitrates.\n</code></pre>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[{"name":"event_loop_policy","time":{"start":1793024424136,"stop":1793024424137,"duration":1},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"tmp_path_factory","time":{"start":1793024428205,"stop":1793024428205,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_reset_pricing_source","time":{"start":1793026